{"id":"asa","name":"Asa","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:asa"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Asa","text":"Physician, son of Abijah and grandson of Rehoboam, was the third king of Judah. He was zealous in maintaining the true worship of God, and in rooting all idolatry, with its accompanying immoralities, out of the land (1 Kings 15:8-14). The Lord gave him and his land rest and prosperity. It is recorded of him, however, that in his old age, when afflicted, he “sought not to the Lord, but to the physicians” (comp. Jer. 17:5). He died in the forty-first year of his reign, greatly honoured by his people (2 Chr. 16:1-13), and was succeeded by his son Jehoshaphat."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H609","lemma":"אָסָא","xlit":"ʼÂçâʼ","gloss":"Asa, the name of a king and of a Levite","kjv":"Asa","count":14,"share":0.61},{"strong":"H1201","lemma":"בַּעְשָׁא","xlit":"Baʻshâʼ","gloss":"Basha, a king of Israel","kjv":"Baasha","count":5,"share":0.22},{"strong":"H7414","lemma":"רָמָה","xlit":"Râmâh","gloss":"Ramah, the name of four places in Palestine","kjv":"Ramah","count":3,"share":0.13},{"strong":"H4427","lemma":"מָלַךְ","xlit":"mâlak","gloss":"to reign","kjv":"consult, indeed, be  king, be  queen","count":4,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H1129","lemma":"בָּנָה","xlit":"bânâh","gloss":"to build","kjv":"build, obtain children, make, repair","count":4,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H4601","lemma":"מַעֲכָה","xlit":"Maʻăkâh","gloss":"Maakah , the name of a place in Syria, also of a Mesopot","kjv":"Maachah, Maachathites. See also H1038","count":2,"share":0.09}],"verses":["1Kgs.15.8","1Kgs.15.9","1Kgs.15.11","1Kgs.15.13","1Kgs.15.14","1Kgs.15.16","1Kgs.15.17","1Kgs.15.18","1Kgs.15.20","1Kgs.15.22","1Kgs.15.23","1Kgs.15.24","1Chr.3.10","1Chr.9.16","1Kgs.15.10","1Kgs.15.12","1Kgs.15.15","1Kgs.15.19","1Kgs.15.21","2Chr.14.0","2Chr.15.0","2Chr.16.0","Matt.1.7"],"related":[{"id":"baasha","type":"cooccur","shared":7,"jaccard":0.149,"why":"7 verses are indexed un